// @expect-error Class 'A' extends 'B', which extends 'A', so 'A' would be its own base class. Remove one of the 'extends' clauses in that chain.
// @expect-error Interface 'Alpha' extends 'Beta', which extends 'Alpha', so 'Alpha' would extend itself. Remove one of the 'extends' clauses in that chain.
// @expect-error build failed with 2 problems
// A cycle of base classes is reported once, on the first class of it. A class declared ahead of
// the cycle that extends a class on it is not on the cycle, so it is not reported. An interface
// that extends one on an interface cycle is not reported either.
class D extends A {
}

class A extends B {
    int a;
}

class B extends A {
    int b;
}

interface Gamma extends Alpha {
}

interface Alpha extends Beta {
}

interface Beta extends Alpha {
}

main() -> int {
    return 0;
}
